{
  "id": "SPEC-RELEASE-PR-DECISION-014",
  "status": "draft",
  "owner_track": "release-security",
  "depends_on": ["SPEC-RELEASE-INTERFACES-013"],
  "purpose": "Move managed release-pull-request policy from the GitHub composite-action shell script into a typed, provider-neutral Callisto decision boundary.",
  "scope": "The credential-free observation, deterministic decision, CLI JSON interface, GitHub snapshot collector, thin GitHub executor, and black-box contract tests for creating, updating, superseding, and retaining a Callisto-managed release PR.",
  "non_goals": [
    "Making a GitHub pull request or its metadata release authority after merge.",
    "Putting forge tokens, raw credentials, shell commands, or arbitrary GitHub API responses in durable release intent/state/receipt records.",
    "Changing the merged-release-commit authority, artifact, or execute contracts from SPEC-RELEASE-INTERFACES-013."
  ],
  "architecture": {
    "observation": "The action gathers a small, credential-free snapshot of the configured repository's open managed PRs and branch workflow-delta facts. Callisto validates that snapshot against explicit configured base/release branch identity; it never accepts caller-side preselection of an existing PR.",
    "decision": "Callisto determines whether pending changesets require no PR, a new canonical PR, an update of exactly one canonical or SHA-suffixed managed PR, or a replacement PR. The decision names exact expected PR number/branch facts so the executor can detect a race before mutation.",
    "execution": "The composite action invokes `callisto release-pr decide`, then only executes the returned operation: version from the current base, stage the resulting worktree changes as a `callisto release-pr commit-plan` and materialize it on a deterministic staging branch via the forge's `createCommitOnBranch` commit API, verify the staged commit's tree is byte-identical to the local `git write-tree` result, move the real managed branch's ref onto that verified commit via a plain REST ref update, create or edit the named PR, and always delete the staging ref afterward. There is no local Git commit or `git push` anywhere in this path. It may render a body, manage a configured label, and re-observe expected state, but it does not independently choose an operation or branch.",
    "authority": "This is pre-merge collaboration policy, not durable release authority. After merge, SPEC-RELEASE-EXECUTION-FOUNDATION-007's parent-to-commit validation remains the sole release authority."
  },
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-001",
      "criterion": "`callisto release-pr decide` accepts an explicit versioned snapshot and explicit configured base/release branch identity, computes whether the workspace has pending changesets, and emits a versioned JSON decision. It is read-only and does not invoke GitHub, push, write manifests, create a PR, tag, publish, or acquire ApplyPermit.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-002",
      "criterion": "The decision model accepts only PRs from the configured repository whose head is either the exact canonical managed branch or its exact lower-case forty-hex SHA-suffixed replacement. Zero eligible PRs yields create; exactly one yields update; more than one fails closed. Lookalike prefixes, foreign repositories, malformed suffixes, a mismatched base branch, duplicate numbers, a PR whose head is the reserved deterministic staging branch itself, or unsupported schema versions fail before any mutation.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-003",
      "criterion": "The commit materialized for an update or create decision always has the snapshot's base commit as its parent, and its change set never contains a `.github/workflows/*` path -- the commit-plan builder refuses such a path, any non-regular-file Git mode (executable bit, symlink, submodule), and any rename, copy, type-change, or unmerged path, all before the commit API is called. A managed branch that was already replaced under the prior SHA-suffixed-branch behavior (a `--<40-hex-sha>` suffix) remains a valid, ordinary managed branch and continues to be recognized and updated in place -- it is not migrated or renamed. A no-pending-changesets decision is a no-op and the executor performs no Git or GitHub mutation.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-004",
      "criterion": "The GitHub action is a thin executor of the Callisto decision: it gathers the snapshot without caller-controlled jq filtering, calls the CLI, branches only on the closed decision kind, and rechecks the decision's expected PR/branch facts immediately before the ref move. Tests execute the exact script with recording Git/GitHub boundaries and demonstrate create, update, retained `--<sha>`-suffixed replacement branch update, no-op, stale-snapshot refusal before any mutation, a moved PR head caught before the ref move, a tree-mismatch refusal, staging-branch cleanup on failure, and that the script never invokes `git push`.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-005",
      "criterion": "The CLI model and action outputs are credential-free, schema-versioned (schema version 2 for the snapshot/action/decision family), and stable for machine consumption. Diagnostics use typed miette errors on invalid snapshots; user-supplied PR body content is not persisted in the decision and remains body-rendering input only.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-006",
      "criterion": "`ReleasePrCommitPlanV1::from_changes` always sets the plan's parent to the snapshot's base commit; it fails closed with a typed error on an empty change set, any `.github/workflows/*` or otherwise unsafe path (`.git/`, `..`, absolute, NUL), any non-regular-file Git mode, any rename/copy/type-change/unmerged path, and a payload over its documented conservative size cap. Each refusal has a dedicated passing test. Byte-fidelity between the plan and the actually-staged commit is proven by comparing the local `git write-tree` result against the staged commit's tree SHA, and this comparison is itself exercised by a passing test.",
      "is_error_case": true
    }
  ],
  "revision_note": "Extracted from SPEC-RELEASE-INTERFACES-013 after review identified that the existing Bash action was rediscovering create/update/supersede policy. This spec narrows the change to pre-merge release-PR collaboration while preserving the already specified post-merge durable authority boundary.\n\nAmended after empirical testing against the real orin-dx/callisto public repository proved the prior supersede-branch mitigation was working around a symptom, not the cause. GitHub's built-in GITHUB_TOKEN cannot write `.github/workflows/*` through either the Git push protocol or the GraphQL `createCommitOnBranch` mutation's own `fileChanges`, on any ref -- confirmed by a real production failure (GitHub Actions run 33679599559, 2026-09-02: \"refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow '.github/workflows/callisto-ci.yml' without 'workflows' permission\"). Supersede's SHA-suffixed replacement branches masked this by cutting a new branch whenever workflow files drifted, causing visible PR churn (#28 closed, #48 opened) with no underlying fix. Direct testing against the real repository confirmed the alternative: `createCommitOnBranch` restricted to only non-workflow paths succeeds (the commit inherits `.github/workflows/*` unchanged from its parent, so the mutation never touches that path), and a subsequent plain REST `updateRef(force)` moving a branch's ref onto that commit also succeeds even when the branch's prior `.github/workflows` content differed from the new commit's inherited content -- with the target branch's `.github/workflows` subtree ending up byte-identical to `main`'s. A ref move is not itself treated as writing `.github/workflows/*` by GitHub's restriction. `Supersede` is removed with no replacement; the commit-plan/staging-branch/ref-move sequence replaces it entirely."
}
